AB  - Chapter 8 discusses the practical implications of adopting a non-medicalised, nondiagnostic approach to distress, unusual experiences and some kinds of troubled or troubling behaviour in the areas of service commissioning, design and delivery, therapeutic practice, research, legal practice, access to welfare and other benefits, and in relation to society as a whole in terms of social policy, equality and social justice. It also illustrates some of the ways in which non-diagnostic practice has already been successfully adopted.
