TI  - Making of a crisis: The political and clinical implications of psychology’s globalization.
AU  - Dhar, Ayurdhi
AU  - Dixit, Sugandh
T2  - Journal of Theoretical and Philosophical Psychology
AB  - This article reveals how the Psy-disciplines are co-opted by neoliberal policies and nationalist ideology in order to reshape people’s experience of themselves. This is done through a critical investigation of the “trauma” and the “hero” narrative as applied to the refugee and orphan conditions. The concept of aproductive suffering is forwarded as a way to understand devastation and distress while resisting neoliberal ethics.
