TI  - Rwanda: gods and ghosts
AU  - Todd, L.
T2  - Seminars in Perioperative Nursing
AB  - This paper provides a personal story. I was born in Africa and have a great empathy for its people. The perceptions I provide are through the eyes of an African born individual who has lived in Australia for many years. It is said that you can take the child out of Africa; however, you cannot take Africa out of the child. During my return to Rwanda in 1994 to 1995, I learned many lessons. Perhaps the most significant being that the Rwandan people displayed absolute stoicism and acceptance of adversity, and from the suffering they had endured, they displayed a great dignity.
