TI  - Returning to history: the ethics of researching asylum seeker health in Australia
AU  - Zion, Deborah
AU  - Briskman, Linda
AU  - Loff, Bebe
T2  - The American journal of bioethics: AJOB
AB  - Australia's policy of mandatory indefinite detention of those seeking asylum and arriving without valid documents has led to terrible human rights abuses and cumulative deterioration in health for those incarcerated. We argue that there is an imperative to research and document the plight of those who have suffered at the hands of the Australian government and its agents. However, the normal tools available to those engaged in health research may further erode the rights and well being of this population, requiring a rethink of existing research ethics paradigms to approaches that foster advocacy research and drawing on the voices of those directly affected, including those bestowed with duty of care for this population.
