AU  - Watego, Chelsea
AU  - Yow Yeh, Kevin
AU  - Nabulsi, Jamal
AU  - Singh, David
AU  - Macoun, Alissa
AU  - Strakosch, Elizabeth
T2  - Journal of International and Intercultural Communication
AB  - In this article, we argue for the power of spite in building a Black-Palestinian antiracist collective driven by Indigenous sovereignty. Reflecting on key moments in our work together in Magandjin/Brisbane, we argue that spite generates sovereign action via its insistence on survival in spite of and to spite the colony. Because this form of antiracism does not require permission it always escapes domestication, and ultimately insists on joy, love and full humanity in the face of violence.
